[Applause]  what the democratic convention  lacked in the usual theater crowds and  balloon drops  it perhaps made up for in familiar faces  welcome to the 2020 democratic national  convention  this was michelle obama's fourth  convention speech  and nearly four years since leaving the  white house  it appeared just as personal for her  when my husband left office  with joe biden at his side we had a  record-breaking  stretch of job creation we'd secured the  right  to health care for 20 million people  four years later the state of this  nation  is very different more than 150  000 people have died and our economy is  in shambles because  of a virus that this president  downplayed for too long  michelle obama endorsed joe biden but  missed the chance to speak  personally about his running mate her  speech  recorded before kamala harris became the  first black woman  to run on the presidential tickets for  the two main parties  an early flaw in the virtual convention  but the finely tuned lineup of speakers  was designed to appeal to a broad  electorate  from twice presidential hopeful bernie  sanders  during this president's term the  unthinkable  has become normal to former republicans  the convention cast a wide net across a  splintered electorate  i'm a lifelong republican but that  attachment holds second place to my  responsibility to my country  that's why i've chosen to appear at this  convention  instead of crowds in the host city  milwaukee  a digital hub is orchestrating online  events around the country  by contrast donald trump is touring  battleground states  as debate rages in washington over his  attacks on the postal service  ahead of an election where millions of  people plan to vote by mail  the only way we're going to lose this  election  is if the election is rigged to remember  that  it's the only way we're going to lose  this election so we have to be very  careful  it's unclear how big an audience this  virtual convention will draw  in the midst of a pandemic with the  country in a state of crisis  people may tune in for far more than  political entertainment  sally lockwood sky news

